{"name":"Tom Thumb","hex":"#4f6348","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tom Thumb","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A fairy-tale character who is the size of a person's thumb; the protagonist and hero of the fairy tale The History of Tom Thumb."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various low-growing wild plants, including meadow vetchling (Lathyrus pratense) and some species of trefoil.","A type of diminutive simple firecracker that explodes to give a loud noise."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tom_Thumb"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tom Thumb","blocks":[{"text":"Tom Thumb is a character of English folklore. The History of Tom Thumb was published in 1621 and was the first known fairy tale printed in English. Tom is no bigger than his father's thumb, and his adventures include being swallowed by a cow, tangling with giants, and becoming a favourite of King Arthur. A metrical version with extensions to the story was completed in about 1700."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Tom_Thumb_Adventures.jpg/330px-Tom_Thumb_Adventures.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Thumb"},{"title":"Tom Thumb (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Tom Thumb is a 1958 British musical fantasy film produced and directed by George Pal, and released by MGM. The film, based on the fairy tale \"Thumbling\" by the Brothers Grimm, is about a tiny youth who manages to outwit two thieves determined to make a fortune from him."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/TomthumbPoster.jpg/330px-TomthumbPoster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Thumb_(film)"},{"title":"Thumb","blocks":[{"text":"The thumb is the first digit of the hand, next to the index finger. When a person is standing in the medical anatomical position, the thumb is the outermost digit. The Medical Latin English noun for thumb is pollex, and the corresponding adjective for thumb is pollical."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Liam_Thumb.jpg/330px-Liam_Thumb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thumb"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Coryats_Crudities.jpg/500px-Coryats_Crudities.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Coryats_Crudities.jpg/500px-Coryats_Crudities.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Title page Coryat's Crudities","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoryats_Crudities.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/FrontispieceTragedyOfTragedies.png/330px-FrontispieceTragedyOfTragedies.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/FrontispieceTragedyOfTragedies.png/330px-FrontispieceTragedyOfTragedies.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Frontispiece The Tragedy of Tragedies","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFrontispieceTragedyOfTragedies.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Tom_Thumb_1888.jpg/330px-Tom_Thumb_1888.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Tom_Thumb_1888.jpg/330px-Tom_Thumb_1888.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Children's edition, 1888","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATom_Thumb_1888.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Tom_Thumb.JPG/500px-Tom_Thumb.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=par